      "text": "\\begin{eqnarray*}3124_{5}=3 \\cdot 5^{3}+1 \\cdot 5^{2} +2 \\cdot 5^{1}+4 \\cdot 5^{0} &=& 3 \\cdot 125+1 \\cdot 25 +2 \\cdot 5+4 \\cdot 1\\\\&=&375+25+10+4\\\\&=&\\boxed{414}\n\\end{eqnarray*}\n\\begin{eqnarray*}3122_{5}=3 \\cdot 5^{3}+1 \\cdot 5^{2} +2 \\cdot 5^{1}+2 \\cdot 5^{0} &=& 3 \\cdot 125+1 \\cdot 25 +2 \\cdot 5+2 \\cdot 1\\\\&=&375+25+10+2\\\\&=&\\boxed{402}\n\\end{eqnarray*}\n\\begin{eqnarray*}124_{5}=1 \\cdot 5^{2}+2 \\cdot 5^{1}+4 \\cdot 5^{0} &=& 1 \\cdot 25+2 \\cdot 5+4 \\cdot 1\\\\&=&25+10+4\\\\&=&\\boxed{39}\n\\end{eqnarray*}\n\nLet's break down the problem step by step and solve it using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we'll calculate each base-5 number to its equivalent in base-10.\n\nThe total amount can be calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total Amount} = 3124_5 + 3122_5 + 124_5\n\\]\n\nEach base-5 number is converted to base-10 and then all the converted values are summed up.\n\nLet's start by converting each number to base-10 and then summing them up in Python.\n\n```python\n# Function to convert a base-5 number to base-10\ndef base5_to_base10(base5_num):\n    base5 = [int(digit) for digit in base5_num]\n    base10_num = 0\n    for i in range(len(base5)):\n        base10_num += base5[i] * (5 ** (len(base5) - i - 1))\n    return base10_num\n\n# Define the base-5 numbers as strings\nnum1_base5 = \"3124\"\nnum2_base5 = \"3122\"\nnum3_base5 = \"124\"\n\n# Convert each number to base-10\nnum1_base10 = base5_to_base10(num1_base5)\nnum2_base10 = base5_to_base10(num2_base5)\nnum3_base10 = base5_to_base10(num3_base5)\n\n# Calculate the total amount in base-10\ntotal_base10 = num1_base10 + num2_base10 + num3_base10\nprint(total_base10)\n```\n```output\n835\n```\nThe total dollar amount that the pirate has accumulated, expressed in base 10, is \\(\\boxed{835}\\).",
